      "claim": "Singapore enacted the Regulation of Imports and Exports (Chewing Gum) Regulations in 1992, which prohibits the import, export, manufacture, sale and offering for sale of chewing gum.",
      "evidence": "Singapore Statutes Online – Regulation of Imports and Exports (Chewing Gum) Regulations, Sec. 2.",
      "weight": 0.4,
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "claim": "The same regulation contains no provision that criminalises the mere possession of chewing gum for personal use or the act of chewing it.",
      "evidence": "Full text of the Regulation of Imports and Exports (Chewing Gum) Regulations lists only commercial activities as offences; there is no clause on possession or consumption.",
      "weight": 0.35,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "claim": "Because the law only targets commercial activities, chewing gum is not illegal per se; it is only illegal to import, sell, manufacture or distribute it.",
      "evidence": "Logical deduction from steps 1 and 2; any act not covered by a criminal provision is not a crime.",
      "weight": 0.25,
      "depends_on": [1, 2]
    }
  ],
